    "title": "Verizon offering payment deferral options for military, federal workers during shutdown - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Jazmine Mills No media credit provided. ,\n1 hours ago\nNEW YORK, N.Y. ( WRBL ) — Telecommunications company Verizon is offering payment relief for military members and federal employees during the government shutdown.\nVerizon customers who are members of the U.S. Military, Coast Guard, first responders and other federal government employees who need more time to pay their bill can call the company and ask about their payment deferral options.\nCustomers will need to provide proof of their employment to qualify.\n“Verizon is dedicated to supporting our customers and the communities we serve,” said Dan Schulman, Verizon CEO. “If federal employees need relief during the shutdown, they can reach out to us and we will keep them connected.”\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to NewsNation.\n1",
